{title: Is There No Longer Wisdom in Teman}
{subtitle: Genesis 36:11; 36:15–42; 1 Chronicles 1:36–53; Jeremiah 49:7–20; Amos 1:11–12; Habakkuk 3:3}
{key: Gm}
{tempo: 72}
{time: 4/4}

{comment: Intro}
| [Gm] | [Gm] | [F] | [Eb] | ×2
| [Gm] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
Eliphaz son of Esau [F]had a firstborn [Eb]son
His name was Teman a[Gm]mong the many listed there
Omar Zepho Ga[F]tam and Kenaz followed him
[Eb]Chiefs descended from the [Gm]mother Adah in [Eb]the land
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
Is [F]there no longer [Gm]wisdom in [Eb]Teman
Coun[F]sel has perished from [Gm]the pru[Eb]dent
Their wisdom has [F]decayed in the [Gm]dust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
He founded a clan in the [F]land of Edom
A [Eb]chief among the people known by [Gm]name
Husham ruled from the land of the [F]Temanites
Before the kings [Eb]of Israel reigned upon the [Gm]throne
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[Eb]Is there no [F]longer wisdom [Gm]in Teman
[Eb]Counsel has [F]perished from the pru[Gm]dent
Their [Eb]wisdom has de[F]cayed in the [Gm]dust
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]Bozrah will become a horror [Gm]and a disgrace
A [F]ruin and a curse forever[Gm]more
The [Eb]pride of the heart has de[Gm]ceived the eagle
Who [F]builds his nest as high as the [Gm]sky
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
[Eb]Leave your or[F]phans I will [Gm]keep them alive
[Eb]Let your wid[F]ows trust in [Gm]me
[Eb]Is there no [F]longer wisdom [Gm]in Teman
{end_of_verse}

